{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 15,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then answered Eliphaz the Temanite, and said,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should a wise man make answer with vain knowledge,\nAnd fill himself with the east wind?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Should he reason with unprofitable talk,\nOr with speeches wherewith he can do no good?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yea, thou doest away with fear,\nAnd hinderest devotion before God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thine iniquity teacheth thy mouth,\nAnd thou choosest the tongue of the crafty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thine own mouth condemneth thee, and not I;\nYea, thine own lips testify against thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Art thou the first man that was born?\nOr wast thou brought forth before the hills?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Hast thou heard the secret counsel of God?\nAnd dost thou limit wisdom to thyself?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What knowest thou, that we know not?\nWhat understandest thou, which is not in us?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With us are both the grayheaded and the very aged men,\nMuch elder than thy father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are the consolations of God too small for thee,Even the word that is gentle toward thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why doth thy heart carry thee away?\nAnd why do thine eyes flash,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That against God thou turnest thy spirit,\nAnd lettest words go out of thy mouth?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "What is man, that he should be clean?\nAnd he that is born of a woman, that he should be righteous?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Behold, he putteth no trust in his holy ones;\nYea, the heavens are not clean in his sight:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How much less one that is abominable and corrupt,\nA man that drinketh iniquity like water!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will show thee, hear thou me;\nAnd that which I have seen I will declare",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Which wise men have told\nFrom their fathers, and have not hid it;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Unto whom alone the land was given,\nAnd no stranger passed among them):",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The wicked man travaileth with pain all his days,Even the number of years that are laid up for the oppressor.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "A sound of terrors is in his ears;\nIn prosperity the destroyer shall come upon him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He believeth not that he shall return out of darkness,\nAnd he is waited for of the sword.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He wandereth abroad for bread, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saying",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", Where is it?\nHe knoweth that the day of darkness is ready at his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Distress and anguish make him afraid;\nThey prevail against him, as a king ready to the battle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because he hath stretched out his hand against God,\nAnd behaveth himself proudly against the Almighty;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He runneth upon him with a ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stiff",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " neck,With the thick bosses of his bucklers;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Because he hath covered his face with his fatness,\nAnd gathered fat upon his loins;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he hath dwelt in desolate cities,\nIn houses which no man inhabited,\nWhich were ready to become heaps;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not be rich, neither shall his substance continue,\nNeither shall their possessions be extended on the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall not depart out of darkness;\nThe flame shall dry up his branches,\nAnd by the breath of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "God’s",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " mouth shall he go away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Let him not trust in vanity, deceiving himself;\nFor vanity shall be his recompense.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "It shall be accomplished before his time,\nAnd his branch shall not be green.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He shall shake off his unripe grape as the vine,\nAnd shall cast off his flower as the olive-tree.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the company of the godless shall be barren,\nAnd fire shall consume the tents of bribery.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.15.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.15.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They conceive mischief, and bring forth iniquity,\nAnd their heart prepareth deceit.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
